[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114998,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoma is a benign bone-forming neoplasm consisting of mature bone, restricted almost exclusively to the jaws and craniofacial bones.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114999,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9180/0 Osteoma</p>\r\n<p>9180/0 Surface (periosteal) osteoma</p>\r\n<p>9180/0 Central (endosteal) osteoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115000,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.Z &amp; XH4818 Benign osteogenic tumours of unspecified site &amp; Osteoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115001,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> exostosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115002,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surface (periosteal) osteoma; central (endosteal) osteoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115003,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "<p >In the jaws, the mandible is more often affected than the maxilla {18154576}. Sinuses are a site of predilection, most commonly the frontal sinus followed by the other sinuses {21820784; 25663319; 18154576}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:52:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115004,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "<p>Central osteomas are often asymptomatic, whereas surface osteomas may present with a slow-growing swelling, facial distortion, or altered dental occlusion. Osteomas in familial adenomatous polyposis often arise near the mandibular angle and may be multiple. Sinus/orbital tumours may present with headache or pain {21820784; 26044223}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Osteomas are dense radiopacities with well-defined margins.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-17T15:12:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115005,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteomas occur over a wide age range but mostly in the third to fifth decades of life, with an equal sex distribution {25663319; 26044223}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115006,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "<p>Unknown</p>\r\n<h5>Genetic factors</h5>\r\n<p>Osteomas may be a manifestation of familial adenomatous polyposis, an autosomal dominant disorder associated with a germline mutation in <em>APC</em> {31070935; 34725446}, and they may be the first manifestation.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-17T15:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115007,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p >Osteomas predominantly affect bone formed by membranous ossification {18154576}, and they have a simple karyotype {31741049}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:52:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115008,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Osteoma appears as a bony mass. Surface osteomas may be widely pedunculated to underlying bone. Central osteomas merge with surrounding intramedullary bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115009,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Osteomas are composed mostly of lamellar bone, compact or trabecular, in which osteoblasts and osteoclasts are usually inconspicuous. Some contain osteoblastoma-like areas that are thought to represent a reactive remodelling process and do not imply more aggressive behaviour {19792048}. As many as 40% of sinus/orbital osteomas contain such areas {25663319}. Fibro-osseous lesions, sclerosing osteomyelitis, and ossification in a fibrous epulis may mimic an osteoma {26044223}.</p>\r\n<p>Lesions of the central (endosteal) subtype of osteoma are also known as bone islands. Unlike surface osteomas, bone islands arise more frequently in long bones and are a mixture of hamartomas and true neoplasms. Rare extraosseous osteoma occurs in soft tissue {26044223}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-01-10T12:45:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115010,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115011,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115012,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> compatible radiological features; surface origin (surface type); mature lamellar bone with solid cortical or medullary patterns.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115013,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115014,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 168,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Growth is slow. Resection is performed for symptomatic osteomas; recurrence is unusual {18154576; 21820784}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:32:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]